        # [CRIT] "his face carved in shadow, his breath held" — PC INTERIORITY: narrates Ossal's physical state and breath control, interior to his conscious control.
        # [CRIT] "There was no sound. No movement. Only the weight of what had been lost—and what might yet come." — PC INTERIORITY: "the weight of what had been lost" and speculative future projection ("what might yet come") are interior to Ossal's consciousness, not stated in RECORD.
